Script_FrameCollisionTest v0.20 loaded.
GENERALIZED ACTOR / WEAPON-SLOT PROTOTYPE.
NO IsPlayer restriction.
NO 2H / Staff / 1H use-type restriction.
NO P0/P1/P2 restriction.
Normal eligibility: exact Attack action + Hit phase + current _Attack_Hit_ motion + RIGHT/LEFT/BOTH source marker.
Quick eligibility: OnAI_QuickAttack + exact Quick/QuickR/QuickL action + Hit phase + a RIGHT/LEFT/BOTH source marker.
Accepted Quick marker completes one-shot callback bookkeeping: StatePosition -> 1.
Full Whirl eligibility: OnAI_WhirlAttack + exact WhirlAttack action + Hit phase + a RIGHT/LEFT/BOTH source marker.
Accepted full-Whirl marker completes one-shot callback bookkeeping: StatePosition -> 1.
Full Whirl uses explicit marker windows; ResetOnUntouch is NOT enabled.
v0.20 PRIMARY-MOTION LIFETIME PROBE: read-only; cleanup behavior is unchanged.
STEP B1 PRIMARYFIRST EVENT PROBE: PlayMotion/StopMotion request/result snapshots; diagnostic-only.
STEP B3 COMBATMOVE STARTRECOVER BOUNDARY PROBE: player-only BEGIN/END snapshots; diagnostic-only.
STEP B4 NATIVE CLEANUP CALL-SITE PROBE: exact player weapon 7 -> 5 caller module/RVA; diagnostic-only.
STEP B5 CLEANUP PARENT-STACK PROBE: short Win32-captured raw stack for exact player weapon 7 -> 5 cleanup; diagnostic-only.
STEP B6 HIT REPLACEMENT STACK PROBE: player PrimaryFirst outgoing attack-Hit replacement stack; diagnostic-only.
v0.20 probe runs only while a marker-owned collision window exists.
Dual SimpleWhirl remains on the original OnAI_SimpleWhirl callback in v0.19.
FIST CAUSAL TEST: raw Fist/PhysicalFist skips SetCollisionGroup(Item_Attack).
FIST CAUSAL TEST: ClearTriggeredList remains active.
G3AB_COL_RIGHT is the final RIGHT equipped-slot marker.
G3AB_COL_LEFT is the final LEFT equipped-slot marker.
G3AB_COL_BOTH is the final BOTH equipped-slot marker.
RIGHT, LEFT, and BOTH use exact-set semantics: the selected source set replaces the previous marker-owned set.
BOTH activates/rearms the right and left equipped slot entities independently at one authored marker.
If any source required by the exact motion is missing, its original attack callback is NOT suppressed.
This protects unarmed/monster attacks until body-source resolution is implemented.
Marker action: non-Fist -> Item_Attack + ClearTriggeredList; Fist -> ClearTriggeredList only.
G3AB_COL_OFF closes only a weapon window opened by this prototype.
OFF requests Item_Equipped and never clears the triggered list.
OFF before ON or after natural reset is consumed as a logged no-op.
Fist/body OFF remains unsupported; Gothic 3 still owns Hit->Recover reset.
Known collision groups: Item_Equipped=5, Item_Attack=7.
PASSIVE DUAL DISCOVERY: Item_Attack transitions are labelled by exact player LEFT/RIGHT slot entity identity.
A Dual both-weapon activation normally appears as separate LEFT and RIGHT transition records.
Preserved RIGHT and LEFT Normal paths passed v0.14 source validation.

v0.19 adds only the full 2H/Staff OnAI_WhirlAttack adapter.
v0.19 preserves the validated v0.18 Normal/Quick RIGHT/LEFT/BOTH/OFF core unchanged.
No Dual SimpleWhirl, Power, collision-source, timing, or cleanup behavior is added in v0.19.
Dedup key: actor + RIGHT/LEFT slot snapshot + motion + marker + action + phase + state time; wall window <= 5 ms.

Authored-occurrence budgets are cached separately for RIGHT, LEFT, BOTH, and OFF.
Budget key: actor + RIGHT/LEFT slot snapshot + motion + action + phase.
Marker-time or controlled-callback state-time rollback starts a new execution.
Natural collision reset outside the owning Hit execution retires the actor budget.
No per-frame actor scan; budget work occurs only when a reserved marker is received.

Installing hooks...
Hooks installed.

